<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI27-BLOCK-005>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI27-BLOCK-005" ;
  triage:title "PR #642 (AI.27/AICH-S7) CI red on all 3 OS legs: new RULE-002 hard violation (dispatch, 118 lines), RULE-003 hard violation (runtime_health.rs prod=1072), and a real test failure (peer sync progress lock poisoned)" ;
  triage:description """Independently verified via `gh pr checks 642` at commit d636a522586943f93a63f8083bcec8d888d4cee7 (branch feature/pAI-s27-peer-delivery-observability, run 30206923692): Just lint (windows/macos/ubuntu-latest) and Test (windows/macos/ubuntu-latest) all FAIL identically on every OS leg; Clippy and Format check pass. Three distinct root causes confirmed by direct local reproduction against a fresh detached checkout of this exact commit:

1. RULE-002 (function-length) new hard violation, confirmed via `python3 scripts/check-function-length.py`: crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health.rs:628-745 `dispatch` (118 lines) -- this is new and overlaps the diff (not the pre-existing grandfathered atm-core/src/observability.rs normalize_json_number violation, which remains unchanged and out of scope). This escalates/refines AI27-ARCH-001 -- that record was written against an earlier commit (5e91a889) before AI.26's forward-merge and further AI.27 work grew `dispatch` past the 80-line hard-fail threshold; AI27-ARCH-001 does not mention this specific function.

2. RULE-003 (file-size) hard violation, confirmed via `python3 .just/check_line_counts.py`: crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health.rs prod=1072 (limit prod<=1000). NOTE: this directly contradicts AI27-ARCH-001's classification as `severity Important ... deferred to phase-end CLEANUP, not gating` -- that assumption is empirically false for the current commit: `just lint` on this branch fails hard (non-zero exit, `lines failed` step) specifically because of this violation, on all 3 OS legs. AI27-ARCH-001 was accurate for its own commit (5e91a889, prod under some other measurement) but the file has since regressed back over the limit -- independently confirmed by team-lead diffing prod-line counts between origin/feature/pAI-s26-peer-write-deadline (prod=843, PASS) and origin/feature/pAI-s27-peer-delivery-observability (prod=1072, FAIL) via the identical `.just/check_line_counts.py` script. This is a real, current, CI-blocking regression, not deferred debt, and AI27-ARCH-001 should be treated as superseded/escalated by this record for the RULE-003 portion (do not additionally dispatch AI27-ARCH-001 separately for this same file).

3. Test failure, confirmed on all 3 OS legs (ubuntu run job 89806645443, macos job 89806645392, windows job 89806645399): `tests::runtime_root::peer_reconciliation::peer_sync_for_one_peer_does_not_hold_the_progress_map_during_another_delivery` FAILED. Panic trace: a background thread first panics at crates/atm-daemon/src/tests/runtime_root/peer_reconciliation.rs:22:18 with `release blocked peer delivery: Timeout`, which poisons a shared mutex; the main test thread then panics at peer_reconciliation.rs:381:10 with `same-peer sync must not wait for the in-flight delivery: AtmError { code: DaemonUnavailable, message: "peer sync progress lock poisoned ... " }`. This reads as a genuine test-harness/production concurrency defect (the test's simulated in-flight delivery legitimately times out and poisons the progress-map lock that peer_sync depends on for its same-peer-does-not-block guarantee), not flakiness -- identical failure on all 3 independent OS runners in the same CI run.""" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "ci-gate" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-26T15:45:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
